From: SWMMU nginx CI proposal
Subject: [PATCH] CI: share a SWMMU nginx rootfs across benchmark matrix

Draft for `.github/workflows/ci.yml` on `ci/uml-nommu`. The rootfs/APK
assembly is performed once, uploaded as an artifact, and downloaded by each
measurement matrix leg. The existing workflow already builds the UML kernel
and base image; this proposal reuses those artifacts. The referenced helper
scripts still need to be added/adapted with the CI workflow owners.

--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -25,1 +25,112 @@ jobs:
 jobs:
+  build_swmmu_nginx_rootfs:
+    # Reuse the current UML build and aports APK artifacts. Rootfs setup is
+    # shared once; each benchmark leg gets its own extracted writable copy.
+    needs: [build_nommu_apks]
+    runs-on: ubuntu-22.04
+    timeout-minutes: 45
+    permissions:
+      contents: read
+    steps:
+      - name: Checkout CI support files
+        uses: actions/checkout@v6
+        with:
+          ref: ci/uml-nommu
+      - name: Download SWMMU APK artifacts
+        uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: aports-nommu-apks
+          path: aports-artifacts
+      - name: Prepare nginx guest rootfs once
+        run: |
+          mkdir -p "$RUNNER_TEMP/swmmu-rootfs"
+          # Install ordinary packages before BusyBox/musl so APK triggers run
+          # with host Alpine tools, then install the NOMMU replacements. Also
+          # create a temporary certificate and static nginx response.
+          .github/workflows/build-swmmu-nginx-rootfs.sh \
+            --apks aports-artifacts \
+            --output "$RUNNER_TEMP/swmmu-rootfs/rootfs.tar"
+      - name: Upload shared rootfs
+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: swmmu-nginx-rootfs
+          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/swmmu-rootfs/rootfs.tar
+          if-no-files-found: error
+
+  nginx_swmmu_benchmark:
+    needs: [build_swmmu_nginx_rootfs, build_uml]
+    runs-on: ubuntu-22.04
+    timeout-minutes: 60
+    strategy:
+      fail-fast: false
+      matrix:
+        worker_processes: [1, 4]
+        connections: [4, 16, 64]
+        include:
+          - worker_processes: 1
+            connections: 4
+            wrk_threads: 2
+          - worker_processes: 1
+            connections: 16
+            wrk_threads: 2
+          - worker_processes: 1
+            connections: 64
+            wrk_threads: 2
+          - worker_processes: 4
+            connections: 4
+            wrk_threads: 2
+          - worker_processes: 4
+            connections: 16
+            wrk_threads: 2
+          - worker_processes: 4
+            connections: 64
+            wrk_threads: 2
+    steps:
+      - name: Checkout CI support files
+        uses: actions/checkout@v6
+        with:
+          ref: ci/uml-nommu
+      - name: Download shared guest rootfs
+        uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: swmmu-nginx-rootfs
+          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/swmmu-rootfs
+      - name: Download SWMMU UML image
+        uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: uml-docker-image-um-nommu-sas
+          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/uml-image
+      - name: Load UML image and extract kernel
+        run: |
+          docker load -i "$RUNNER_TEMP/uml-image/uml-image.tar"
+          cid=$(docker create uml-ci/alpine:3.20.3-um-nommu-sas)
+          docker cp "$cid:/root/vmlinux" "$RUNNER_TEMP/vmlinux"
+          docker rm "$cid"
+          mkdir -p rootfs
+          tar -xf "$RUNNER_TEMP/swmmu-rootfs/rootfs.tar" -C rootfs
+      - name: Run nginx smoke test and wrk sample
+        env:
+          WORKERS: ${{ matrix.worker_processes }}
+          CONNECTIONS: ${{ matrix.connections }}
+          WRK_THREADS: ${{ matrix.wrk_threads }}
+        run: |
+          mkdir -p "output/w${WORKERS}-c${CONNECTIONS}"
+          # Harness boots the writable rootfs copy with zpoline=1 seccomp=on,
+          # passes CAP_SYS_RAWIO and CAP_SYS_PTRACE, starts nginx, checks HTTP
+          # and TLS locally, then runs wrk from a separate network container.
+          .github/workflows/run-swmmu-nginx-benchmark.sh \
+            --kernel "$RUNNER_TEMP/vmlinux" \
+            --rootfs rootfs \
+            --workers "$WORKERS" \
+            --threads "$WRK_THREADS" \
+            --connections "$CONNECTIONS" \
+            --duration 30 \
+            --output "output/w${WORKERS}-c${CONNECTIONS}"
+      - name: Upload raw measurements and plot data
+        if: always()
+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: swmmu-nginx-w${{ matrix.worker_processes }}-c${{ matrix.connections }}
+          path: output/
+          if-no-files-found: warn
+
Notes before applying:

1. Add/adapt `build-swmmu-nginx-rootfs.sh` and
   `run-swmmu-nginx-benchmark.sh`. Keep the rootfs as one shared artifact, but
   extract a fresh writable copy in every matrix job.
2. The current `build_nommu_apks` artifact contains BusyBox and musl only.
   Extend its build step to add instrumented OpenSSL, nginx, and coreutils APKs
   from the pinned aports revision, preserving package signatures and the
   matching GCC/plugin provenance.
3. The benchmark matrix is intentionally ordinary push CI, matching the
   existing `benchmark` job style. It tests worker counts and connection counts
   under each same wrk condition; publish results before considering thresholds.
4. The current NOMMU UML build is uniprocessor. Keep workers=4 as a measured
   comparison, but do not expect it to scale like a multi-CPU server.
